      "answerSpaceMm": 18,
      "answer": {
        "short": "$1-(p+q)$. Correct answer: C.",
        "worked": "Since A and B are mutually exclusive, $P(A\\cap B)=0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(A'\\cap B')&=1-P(A\\cup B)\\\\P(A'\\cap B')&=1-[P(A)+P(B)]\\\\P(A'\\cap B')&=1-(p+q)\\end{align*}$$\nCorrect answer: C.",
